  "title": "Lascaux Cave",
  "summary": "Lascaux is a decorated cave near Montignac in the Dordogne, southwestern France, found on 12 September 1940 by four boys after their dog fell down a foxhole. Its Upper Palaeolithic art, dated to about 17,000 to 15,000 BCE, includes close to 600 paintings, mostly of animals, and around 1,400 engravings.",
